# Author: Tigany Zarrouk (tiganyzarrouk@gmail.com)
#
# 3072 orientations, far more than a spectrum needs, because a tilt-strain
# finite difference sees one off-diagonal element of sum r (x) f while the
# reported stress is its symmetric half. The two differ by the quadrature's
# torque, which falls as 1/N: 2.3e-2 of the shear at 48, 1.4e-3 at 768. The
# test converges the quadrature rather than loosening the tolerance.
compute t   all mad/property/python madlib_models ncomp 6 cutoff 3.0 &
            config "backend=callable fn=mad_tensor_toy:tensor types=C,O quantity=tensor6"
fix     mad all mad/nmr/aniso c_t target data/nmr_aniso_target.dat &
            range 75.0 95.0 101 sigma 0.5 orientations 3072 &
            reference 100.0 slope 1.0 gamma 30.0
